 ``--record``: tools/zig/triton_aot_manifest.py's Recorder logs every Triton specialization and EXL3 extension call;
 at the end the manifest and aot_pack.py turn the Triton cache into aot.json + cubins/ (the kernel set the Zig engine
-loads). ``--fixtures``: per window, each layer's output rows, cache rows written, selections and end-of-layer
+loads). ``--fixtures``: per window, each layer's output rows, cache rows, selections and end-of-layer
 scratch (diagnostics) as safetensors, plus meta.json (frozen env, tiles, versions, weight digests).
 
+``TF_GLM53_DSPARK=<dir>`` (the DSpark drafter's checkpoint, the serve's ``TF_GLM53_DSPARK``): after the two chains a
+third, dspark chain runs the drafter itself — tap passes at every chunk size the serve's tap feeding uses (1..64 rows:
+decode rounds chunk at the block, prompt chunks at the drafter's 64-row tap_in), one block pass (``propose``, the
+serve's draft step; the block is always whole — the depth / confidence cut only trims the host chain's candidate list,
+never a launch shape), then verify windows of every width the runner captures (1..block + 1 and the copy widths 8 and
+16) — so every Triton kernel the drafter launches at its real shapes lands in the pack (the static needs enumeration
+cannot see drafter launches; cuda_draft.zig's ``enumerate`` is this chain's mirror). Tap values are zeros: the pack
+needs shapes, not bits (and only the first ``--layers`` layers are loaded, so the later tap columns would be zero
+anyway). Without the env the capture is unchanged.
+
 Must run inside the GLM-5.3 TP4 image (torch, Triton 3.7, the EXL3 extensions build on first use) with
 PYTHONPATH at the champion source's ``src`` and TRITON_CACHE_DIR set to a fresh directory (for ``--record``).
 Usage: see tools/glm53/README.md.
